  {
    "id": "poetry-05",
    "slug": "poem-05",
    "historical_number": "5",
    "text": "Is the freedom to buy things, really the independence we should\nall strive for? Or is it the perspective of an immortal that knows,\nthe earth is our Mother we own nothing on her, she is good and\ngraceful and where we roam on her we are fed",
