    "id": "poetry-09",
    "slug": "poem-09",
    "historical_number": "10",
    "text": "my stomach is growling\nonly I can take care of me\nI am tired\nI can’t pack up everything on my own\nlike I need your help\nI can pack up my stuff\nbut not yours too\nI’ve been hungry\nyou ate all the food without me\nyou care though that I can see",
