  {
    "id": "poetry-16",
    "slug": "poem-16",
    "historical_number": "15",
    "text": "Mirror parallel universes\nwhen i stare into the silver haze not only my current face comes to\nmeet my gape. occasionally, i see crying. i see the tears caused by\nlove affair washed down the sink. i see smiles and healing. i see\nspeeches i've yet to give. i see myself getting older. i see it, all being\nok.",
