  {
    "id": "poetry-21",
    "slug": "poem-21",
    "historical_number": "20",
    "text": "to my mother\nI have four kids.\nyou wore it like a badge.\nI was five\nhelping raise the twins.\nyou crawled into my bed.\nyour father was dead.\nvodka and crying.\nI made room.\nin Texas\nI woke to my cousin\nin my boyfriend’s bed.\nhe beat me.\nlocked me in a closet.\nyou knew\nand posted about her\non Facebook.\nyou chose her.\nwhen your father died\nI held you.\nwhen mine died\nyou turned everyone\nagainst me.\nhe was the only one\nin that family\nwho loved me.\nyou knew that too.\nmy brothers followed you.\nI lost my father\nand somehow\nI was the thing\neveryone needed\nto get away from.\na triangle.\nthe evil eye inside.\nI need a reminder\non my skin\nthat you lie.\nI still want\nto believe my mother.\nyou lied.\nsaid I only wanted money.\nmade me the problem\nso nobody had to look\nat what you did.\nyou knew.\nmy father was dead.\nI wanted my mother.\nI have four kids.\nI can still hear you\ntelling people.\nI am one of them.\nwhen you cried\nI made room in my bed.\nwhen I told you I was hurt\nyou said\nyou didn’t want to hear.",
    "text_sha256": "f3275b753e9fe37c2ca7d0998be84dd6ac1da70edb8640c630ac81ae7b2ee7a9",
    "author": "Chloe Starr",
    "source": "script.js: originalPoetry.poems",
    "creation_date": null,
    "original_publication_date": null,
    "visibility": "public",
    "writing_state": "published",
    "film": {
      "state": "not_registered"
    },
    "presentation": {
      "tone": "paper",
      "scale": "intimate"
    },
    "source_entry_index": 20,
    "source_text_sha256": "f3275b753e9fe37c2ca7d0998be84dd6ac1da70edb8640c630ac81ae7b2ee7a9",
    "versions": [
